# ArduPlane Parameters - Mini Talon Airspeed Overlay (Tier 2 diagnostic: windmax0)
# Apply on top of plane_base.parm for Gazebo wind / pitot worlds.
#
# Envelope/mechanism matrix cell (ADR-0016): TIER 2 DIAGNOSTIC.
# Identical to config/overlays/plane_airspeed.parm EXCEPT AHRS_WIND_MAX, which is
# set to 0 to DISABLE the AHRS believed-airspeed clamp on both the sensor path
# and the EKF synthetic path (libraries/AP_AHRS/AP_AHRS.cpp:985 and :1057, both
# gated on _wind_max > 0). With the clamp off, the believed airspeed (CTUN.As)
# should track the raw reported airspeed (ARSP.Airspeed) instead of being pinned
# at ground_speed + AHRS_WIND_MAX.
#
# PURPOSE: diagnostic mechanism probe -- "what does TECS do if it receives the
# full lie?" This is NOT a safety or real-stack claim. The protected real stack
# uses AHRS_WIND_MAX = 15 (plane_airspeed.parm).
#
# MANDATORY VALIDATION (ADR-0016 sec. 4): the first Tier 2 run is a mechanism
# verification flight. ARSPD_WIND_GATE=5 and the EKF airspeed innovation gate are
# independent of AHRS_WIND_MAX and may still reject/bound the lie. The mechanism
# gate (tests/.../mechanism_gate.py) must confirm CTUN.As tracks ARSP.Airspeed
# before any "TECS fully believes the lie" claim is made.
#
# One-source rule:
# - Gazebo provides wind
# - SITL wind remains disabled

ARSPD_TYPE       100       # JSON airspeed sensor from Gazebo / ArduPilotPlugin
ARSPD_USE        1
ARSPD_AUTOCAL    0         # Do not learn offset from live wind on startup
ARSPD_SKIP_CAL   1         # Keep startup from zeroing in active wind
ARSPD_OFFSET     0

# Baseline 14/10/22 envelope; only AHRS_WIND_MAX changes vs. plane_airspeed.parm.
AIRSPEED_CRUISE  14
AIRSPEED_MIN     10
AIRSPEED_MAX     22
STALL_PREVENTION 1

SIM_WIND_SPD     0
SIM_WIND_DIR     180
SIM_WIND_TURB    0
AHRS_WIND_MAX    0         # TIER 2: clamp disabled (vs. 15 in the protected stack)
